# Muerra, Trash Tactician: one payment can expend 4 and expend 8 at once (CR 700.14). Muerra is cast on turn one; on turn
# three its first-main-phase trigger adds one mana for its one Raccoon, and from no mana spent yet that turn, Fireball with X
# = 7 spends eight - from below four to eight, so both abilities trigger from that payment: its caster gains 3 life, and
# the top two cards of their library are exiled. Of those, the Plains is played on their next turn, turn five; Memnite,
# left in exile, can't be cast on turn seven, as the permission ended with turn five (CR 514.2, 611.2a).

